  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Public administration is the machinery and process of implementing public policy. Public finance is the revenue side, private management is a different sector, and elections are a separate process.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Tax funding and political accountability are the distinguishing marks. Profit is the private test, and citizens cannot choose their government's services in the way customers choose a firm.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Permanent officials who advise, prepare policy and administer departments. Ministers are political, judges are judicial, and party officers are outside the service.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The administrative class is one of the four tiers, with the professional, executive-clerical and support classes. The others are not parts of the service.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The permanent secretary is the administrative head and the accounting officer, while the minister is the political head. The distinction is a favourite examination point.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Permanence means continuity: the government changes, the service remains, and its knowledge is not lost at every election.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The minister answers publicly; the official stays out of the public argument. It does not mean the official is anonymous to the service or barred from voting.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Impartiality is equal service to the government of the day, not neutrality about policy inside the service and not a ban on private opinion.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Merit is the canon, with the Federal Character Commission policing diversity alongside it. The tension between the two is a standard examination question.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Federal Civil Service Commission handles appointment, promotion and discipline. The National Assembly appropriates, and the courts review.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Udoji reviewed structure and pay, and its 1974 awards raised salaries and introduced a unified grading structure.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Oronsaye recommended rationalising agencies, and its report remains the standard example of a cost-of-governance exercise.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A corporation is created by law, owned by the state, and given its own board and accounts. A public limited company is privately owned, and a department is not a separate legal body.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A corporation needs a legal instrument. Under military rule that instrument was a decree; under a civilian constitution it is an Act.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Large capital, natural monopoly, strategic sectors and social service are the reasons. Profit for shareholders is the private-company motive.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Overstaffing, politicisation and losses are the standard problems. The corporations are usually subsidised, and they do have boards.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Privatisation moves ownership to the private sector. Nationalisation is the reverse, and commercialisation keeps ownership public.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Commercialisation is about the discipline of cost recovery, not ownership. Privatisation changes the owner.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Deregulation opens a sector to private operators by removing restrictive rules. It does not mean the absence of regulation.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The third tier, after the federal and state governments. It is the level closest to the people.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The statutory allocation is the main source, with state allocations, internal revenue and grants. Company tax, import duty and royalties are federal.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Sanitation, markets, local roads and primary school support are local functions. Defence, coinage and treaties are federal.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Councils depend on allocations they do not control, and their internal revenue is weak. The problem is dependence, not excess.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Dissolution and caretaker committees remove the council's elected autonomy. By-laws, rates and elections are the council's own functions.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It investigates complaints of maladministration and recommends remedies. It is not a court, does not prosecute, and is independent of the police.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Commission reports and recommends; it cannot enforce. That is the standard criticism of the Nigerian ombudsman.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Bureau receives declarations and refers a breach to the Code of Conduct Tribunal. Auditing belongs to the Auditor-General, and elections to INEC.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Auditor-General audits and reports to the legislature. Tax collection belongs to the FIRS, the budget to the executive, and appointments to the commission.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The EFCC and ICPC are law-enforcement bodies; the ombudsman investigates maladministration and recommends. None of the three is a court.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The legislature controls through appropriation, questions and summons. Appointment, promotion and transfer are executive functions.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The courts can quash an unlawful administrative act and award damages. The budget is legislative, and appointments are executive.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Head of the Civil Service of the Federation is the professional head. The Secretary to the Government is a different office, and the President is the political head of the executive.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The minister carries political responsibility and the permanent secretary carries administrative responsibility as accounting officer. Neither is elected.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Permanence is continuity, not supremacy: the service advises and implements, while the elected government decides.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A ministry is a department of the executive; a parastatal or corporation has separate legal personality, a board and accounts, created by law.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The efficiency and fiscal-burden argument drove the programme. Critics reply that privatisation can transfer a monopoly to private owners without creating competition.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Bureau polices the conduct of public officers. The others are a corporation, an appointing body and a statistical agency.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Delay, corruption and resistance to change are the standard criticisms. The service is rule-bound rather than rule-free, and it has many ministries rather than few.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The reform sought to make the service more responsive by politicising the top, and it was widely criticised for weakening the anonymity and impartiality of the service.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The TSA brings ministries, departments and agencies into one account at the Central Bank so that cash is visible and leakages are reduced. It does not abolish the service or replace the audit function.
  ]

]

